WEBVTT

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:04.400
Detection engineering is the practice of designing, building, testing, deploying,

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.972
and maintaining security detections that identify suspicious activity.

00:00:07.972 --> 00:00:09.980
A detection is the logic, context,

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:14.000
and operational workflow that turns telemetry into a signal defenders can use.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:16.970
Good detections help teams focus attention where it matters most.

00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:21.000
They connect observable behavior to a meaningful question, such as whether an account,

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:22.000
workload, host, application,

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:25.190
or cloud resource is behaving in a way that deserves investigation.

00:00:25.190 --> 00:00:28.995
Detection engineering is not measured by the number of alerts generated.

00:00:28.995 --> 00:00:31.960
An alert is only useful when it provides enough relevance, context,

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:34.960
and confidence for an analyst or automation to make a better decision.

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:38.010
The discipline matters because defenders operate under constraints.

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:42.075
Time, attention, telemetry quality, and business context are limited,

00:00:42.075 --> 00:00:45.750
so detection work must reduce noise while improving the organization’s ability to identify

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:47.000
suspicious activity.
